WEBVTT

00:00.080 --> 00:01.680
So now what is a data flow diagram?

00:01.680 --> 00:07.840
We can draw a simple visual in order to map the flow of your data, where it comes from and where it

00:07.840 --> 00:08.360
ends up.

00:08.360 --> 00:14.120
So you want just to make clear how the data flows through different layers of your projects and thus

00:14.120 --> 00:16.920
help us to create something called the data lineage.

00:16.920 --> 00:20.320
And this is really nice, especially if you are analyzing an issue.

00:20.320 --> 00:25.160
So if you have like multiple layers and you don't have a real data lineage or flow, it's going to be

00:25.160 --> 00:29.960
really hard to analyze the scripts in order to understand the origin of the data.

00:29.960 --> 00:33.640
And having this diagram can improve the process of finding issues.

00:33.640 --> 00:35.640
So now let's go and create one okay.

